{
  "case_id": "2008-08-22",
  "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:15 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Theodore B. Olson, Esq.",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A fair trial in a fair tribunal is a fundamental constitutional right. That means not only the absence of actual bias, but a guarantee against even the probability of an unfair tribunal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Who says? Have we ever held that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Theodore B. Olson, Esq.",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "would come to the conclusion -- knowing all of the facts, would come to the conclusion that a judge or jurist would probably be biased against that individual or in favor of his opponent, that would be sufficient under the Due Process Clause, we submit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The contribution limit in West Virginia is $1,000. Mr. Blankenship contributed $1,000, and then he put up three million additional dollars, three thousand"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Are the States -- are the States really free to do that? We have recognized First Amendment interests in participating in the electoral process before."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So you think the Constitution might have been violated if Starcher -- you think due process might have been violated if that judge had remained on the bench?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Frey",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Court has recognized that where a judge is embroiled with a litigant, and has a personal animosity arising out of the relationship with the litigant, that is a -- that is possible ground for recusal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Frey",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Let me say just one point about probability of bias, which is conceptually -- the rule is quite clear at common law, as the Court knows, that that was not a ground for disqualification of a judge."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why is probability in this context any more difficult to figure out than probability in the Fourth Amendment context?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We have no choice with regard to the reasonableness standard. We -- it's not a standard we made up."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Frey",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0002-0005",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The plaintiffs' lawyers gave a million and a half dollars to Justice McGraw to support his reelection. Suppose he had won? What do you do?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Frey",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the principle is either debt of gratitude or hope of future benefit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If one is going to go into that calculation, one is going to assume that in eight years, there's going to be another three million dollars waiting to be spent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And then debt of gratitude -- we keep asking but your time is running out, have you said what you need to say on debt of gratitude?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Specifically if Justice Benjamin were term limited, would this case be different?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Olson",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0002-0011",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "is from the Tumey case, might not a defendant with reason say that he would fear he would not get a fair trial. So instead of the question that my opponent asks, would you be fair, which is not the standard because actual bias isn't the test, would there be a perception, likelihood, probability appearance of bias, to use the language used by this Court over and over again."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Is that a reasonable person that's making that inquiry, is that the standard?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Okay. Would a reasonable person think it's a ground for recusal if the lawyer and the judge were very close friends?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Opponents",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our opponents say there's -- bias tribunals are not prohibited by the Due Process Clause nor probably biased or the appearance of bias. We think there has to be some constitutional limit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3a3a7caf9f5f668cb088995e482e2d2504057ee615c5b469c2ec301f348b631f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3a3a7caf9f5f-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-08-22",
      "confidence": 0.0,
